.POST SPRUCE.
Post spruce, "asentokuusi" in UnReal language, is the simplest and easiest-to-make form of a temporary shelter. 
It's not an actual dwelling but used for resting and sleeping protected from the elements.<br>
  This simple shelter is made by felling a spruce tree to lean against another spruce tree.
Some low branches are cut to make space in the midst of the trees, and the cut twigs are laid on the ground as insulation.<br> 
  Post spruces are used all year round when temporary protection from the rain, snow or cold is needed. 
During cold seasons, especially in the winter, a decent campfire is made right beside your post to stay nicely warm.
***

.TERRAIN.
