.BREAM.BREAMS.
The bream is a relatively common fish living in the inland lakes and slow flowing rivers.
Breams prefer large lakes and tend to move in swarms. They are usually caught using nets,
but can also be caught with a common fishing rod.<br>
<br>
During their spawning season, breams can also be caught by spear fishing. 
Much like pikes, breams also spawn at vegetation rich, shallow shoreline waters. 
Spawning breams are easily spotted in the shallow waters and can be speared or scooped
into a lippo from the shore.<br>
<br>
Spawning of the bream usually takes place from seedtime to fallow month when the water
is suitably warm for the purpose. The spawning happens in cycles that can last for quite a long time.
***


// added & proofred Sep-09-2023
//
.SALMON.SALMONS.
Salmon is a large and valued migratory fish that can be encountered in rivers and
inland lakes, as well as in the sea and coastal areas. As a migratory fish, salmon
travels through the rivers.<br>
<br>
  Salmons hatch in freshwater headstreams and spend their juvenile years in rivers and lakes.
Upon maturing, they migrate to the sea, and return back to rivers to spawn. It is said that
salmons return to spawn in the very same river that they originated from.<br>
<br>
  During the salmon migration and spawning they are caught from the rivers and rapids especially
well with a lippo. Salmon migrates from the sea up the rivers throughout the summer.
They do dwell in the rivers until the spawning starts in late autumn, usually around
fall or dirt month. The actual spawning time depends on the water temperature which needs to be
fairly cold for the salmons to start their spawning. When the spawning starts, it lasts for a few weeks.<br>
***

// added & proofread Sep-22-2023
//
.LAVARET.LAVARETS.
The lavaret is a diverse fish species with distinct populations living in different environments,
with slightly differing appearances and habits. Lavarets are commonly found in lakes throughout
the UnReal World, but are also present in rivers and the sea.<br>
<br>
  Like salmon, the lavaret also spawns in late autumn. For the lavaret, this happens between fall month and dead month,
depending on the water temperature. The waters need to be fairly cold for the lavarets to start their spawning.<br>
<br>
  Different lavaret populations spawn in different places. Some migrate upstream to spawn in rivers, whereas some
spawn in the sea or in lakes by the rocks, skerries and shores. In all waters, the lavaret spawning takes
place in relatively shallow water, and during this period they are commonly caught when lippo fishing.
