//
.BRONZE BALL PENDANT.
A hollow bronze ball, usually a little less than an inch in diameter. The ball is decorated with embossed pebbles, forming lines round the ball.
The ball hangs from a thin bronze chain. This type of pendant is sold by the foreign traders and worn by women of western cultures.
***

.UTILITY ARTICLES.
Some of these items are descriped here:
 SALT, POT.
***

.SALT.
Salt is used in cookery, e.g. in the making of salted meat/fish.
***

// updated 24.3.2025
//
.POT.
Pot is a cooking vessel made of iron, used in cookery for preparing food. 
It has a deep, round shape with high sides and is designed to hold liquids or ingredients while cooking over heat. 
Pots can be used for cooking over an open flame, on hot coals, or in a fireplace, making them suitable for all types of cooking.<br>
    An iron pot is a durable cooking tool that can last a lifetime, but if an iron pot is not affordable or available, 
a birch-bark pot, suitable for wilderness situations, can be used as an alternative.
***

// added 24.3.2025
//
.BIRCH-BARK POT.
Birch-bark pot is a traditional cooking vessel made from a single sheet of birch bark, carefully shaped into a rectangular form.
The seams of the bark are sealed tightly by pressing the edges together with short pieces of twigs, which are split at one end to hold the bark in place. 
This design allows the pot to hold liquids, such as water, and be used for cooking over an open fire.<br>
    It is essential to manage the heat carefully to prevent the bark from catching fire, ensuring that the water heats up without damaging the pot.
While the birch-bark pot is a lightweight and practical solution for cooking in the wild, it is naturally less durable than an iron pot and can only be used a limited number of times. 
Its smaller size also limits the number of portions you can cook at one go.
***

