.SEWING NEEDLE.IRON SEWING NEEDLE.BONE SEWING NEEDLE.
Sewing needle is a fundamental tool for making and repairing clothes. The most handy sewing needles are made of iron
by blacksmiths, but they can be also crafted from animal bone. 
***

.FISHHOOK.HOOK.WOODEN FISHHOOK.BONE FISHHOOK.
Fishhook is attached to the line of a fishing rod and it is the part that actually catches the fish.
Fishhooks can be made of wood, bone and iron. Iron hooks are the best kind, then come the bone hooks. 
Wooden hooks are the least effective and usually relied on only in survival situation.<br>
<br>
   Fishhooks may snap off as the line wears out from use, especially around the hook. 
This wear is relative to the number and size of the fish that have nibbled the line over time.
You can use a spare fishhook to repair a fishing rod with no hook. First [a]pply the fishhook, and then select a fishing rod to repair.<br>
If you wish to remove a fishhook from a fishing rod then [a]pply a fishing rod when you are on dry land away from open water.<br>
***


// added Jun-10-2023
//
.NETTING NEEDLE.
Netting needle is a wooden tool used to make nets. It is quite simple but essential tool that allows 
weaving the net with proper knots and forming a tightly fastened mesh of uniform size.
***

// added Mar-16-2021
//
.SPINDLE.
A spindle is a tool made from wood used for spinning plant fibres into yarn.<br>
All the fibre processing is carried out by using your TEXTILECRAFT skill.
***


// added & proofred Aug-29-2023
//
.LIPPO.
Lippo is a kind of a dip net used for catching fish from rapids and shallow waters.
Fishing with a lippo is especially effective only at certain times of the
year; when the fish to be caught are migrating upstream to their spawning locations, and during the
active spawning period.
Thus, the most common fish that are caught with the lippo, are the migratory salmon and lavaret.<br>
<br>
  A Lippo is constructed in such a way that it has a wooden hoop into which multiple small birch saplings are tied to.
These saplings are tied together at their open ends, so that they form a net like construction around the hoop.
The hoop with a net is then fixed to a long wooden pole.<br>
<br>
  Fishing with a lippo in the rivers and rapids is done by standing on rocks in the river. The location is 
often suitable when there are several rocks around as these are the usual places where both resting and
spawning river fish are around and can be caught.<br>
  The lippo is lowered into the water, down to the bottom, and carefully dragged around in order to catch
resting or spawning fish into its hoop. Successful lippo fishing is greatly based on knowledge of the
locations where the fish might dwell. Start using your lippo either by using the fishing skill or by applying the
lippo from the inventory.<br>
<br>
Additionally, a lippo can also be used from the shore to catch spawning pikes or breams.
***

// added & updated Jan-23-2016
// proofred Aug-31-2023
//
.FISHING ROD.
A common tool for active fishing. You can start angling with a fishing rod either by using the 
fishing skill or by applying the fishing rod from the inventory. Although it is not necessary to bait the fishhook when you start an
angling session, an empty hook is far less attractive to nibble on, than one with a bit of food.<br>
<br>
   You can use pretty much any food item as a bait. 
Predatory fish species favour raw meat and fish, but for example crumbs of bread may also work with some fish.
You can also use a whole small fish, eg. roach or perch, in order to attract a bigger predatory fish.<br>
<br>
   The type of fish caught when rod fishing is quite dependant on the baits used. It's not likely that you'll
catch a pike with an empty hook, but having a small roach as bait might work. And that small roach may have
been caught with quite moderate bait, such as bread crumbs, or even with some tasty vegetation. 
***

// added & updated Jul-01-2023
// proofred Aug-31-2023
//
.NET.NETS.
Nets are tools for passive fishing. They are set and left in the water for a day or two, and then retrieved hopefully 
with some fish caught in it. A common net in the game is about 8 meters long and 2 meters deep with a 5 centimeter mesh. 
This is a size a lone fisher can easily handle.<br>
<br>
Nets can be set either by using the fishing skill or by applying the net from the inventory.
To retrieve a net you can simply pick it up.<br>
<br>
Every time a net is set and retrieved it wears out a bit, and the bigger the catch, the more
it can damage the net. How fast a net wears out depends greatly on your fishing skills. 
A talented fisher can handle the net so that it doesn't get tangled upon setting or retrieving, or unnecessarily
damaged upon releasing the fish. A novice fisherman is prone to handle the net in a more clumsy fashion which
results in more wear and tear.<br>
<br>
Making a net is a laborious task and they were usually woven indoors during wintertime. 
Yarn is naturally required in substantial amounts, and some stronger cordage for the supporting structure, as well
as the float and weight lines. The floats were usually made of birch-bark and rocks were used as weights. 
In the finest nets, the rock weights were wrapped in birch-bark pockets for a more durable construction.
***


